To create glowing text with an animated rainbow gradient border using only HTML and CSS, you can use either a simulated border with a gradient background and padding, or use CSS `border-image` with an animated gradient. The glowing effect is achieved with `text-shadow`. Here’s a complete example:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>Glowing Rainbow Text</title>
  <style>
    body {
      background: #111;
      min-height: 100vh;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      margin: 0;
    }
    .rainbow-border {
      padding: 16px 32px;
      border-radius: 16px;
      background: linear-gradient(90deg, red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo, violet, red);
      background-size: 400% 400%;
      animation: rainbow 6s linear infinite;
      display: inline-block;
    }
    @keyframes rainbow {
      0% { background-position: 0% 50%; }
      50% { background-position: 100% 50%; }
      100% { background-position: 0% 50%; }
    }
    .glow-text {
      background: #111;
      border-radius: 12px;
      color: #fff;
      font-size: 3rem;
      font-weight: bold;
      padding: 20px 40px;
      text-align: center;
      text-shadow:
        0 0 10px #fff,
        0 0 20px #fff,
        0 0 40px #ff00de,
        0 0 80px #ff00de;
      /* Optional: add a subtle box-shadow for more glow */
      box-shadow: 0 0 40px 10px #ff00de44;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="rainbow-border">
    <span class="glow-text">Glowing Rainbow Text</span>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
```

**Explanation:**
- The `.rainbow-border` uses a linear gradient background animated with keyframes to create a moving rainbow border effect. Padding and border-radius create the border illusion.
- The `.glow-text` uses multiple `text-shadow` layers for a glowing effect.
- The background of the text is set to match the page background to make the border stand out.

**Alternative:** You can use `border-image` with a conic-gradient and animate the angle, but browser support for animating `border-image-source` is limited and may not work in all browsers.

