### Problem Understanding

Given a string of length n (even), where all odd positions are missing (represented as '_') and all even positions are known brackets ('(' or ')'), we are to fill in the odd positions with brackets to form a valid regular bracket sequence (RBS) with minimum cost. The cost is the sum of the distances between each matching pair of brackets.

### Key Observations

- The cost of an RBS is `sum of (j - i)` for each matching pair (i, j), where i < j.
